/docker-46","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#host-setup-relax-the-ptrace-policy","content":"**Do this before starting the container, otherwise hook injection will fail at runtime.**"},"253":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-47","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#host-setup-relax-the-ptrace-policy","content":"SnowLuma's native addon uses `ptrace` to inject the hook into the in-container QQ process. Modern Linux distros (Ubuntu / Debian / Arch / …) ship with `kernel.yama.ptrace_scope` set to `1` or higher, which means **even with `--cap-add=SYS_PTRACE` on the container, the host kernel still blocks the ptrace call**."},"254":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-48","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#host-setup-relax-the-ptrace-policy","content":"Run **once** on the host:"},"255":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-49","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#host-setup-relax-the-ptrace-policy","content":"Verify:"},"256":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-50","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#host-setup-relax-the-ptrace-policy","content":"Writing to `/etc/sysctl.d/99-snowluma-ptrace.conf` keeps the setting across reboots. If your host has stricter security requirements (multi-tenant, internet-facing), prefer a dedicated isolated host (bare metal / VM) over relaxing the system-wide policy."},"257":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-51","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#one-line-docker-run","content":"`--cap-add=SYS_PTRACE` and `--security-opt seccomp=unconfined` are **mandatory**. SnowLuma's native addon uses ptrace to inject the hook into the QQ process; the default seccomp profile blocks that."},"258":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-52","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#one-line-docker-run","content":"`--shm-size=1g` is needed for QQ's Chromium runtime — the defau