me password:"},"305":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-99","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#finding-the-webui-bootstrap-password","content":"Just the password string:"},"306":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-100","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#finding-the-webui-bootstrap-password","content":"The bootstrap password is logged **only on a brand-new data volume's first boot**. Reusing the volume or restarting won't regenerate it."},"307":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-101","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#running-multiple-qq-accounts","content":"Linux QQ ships a single-instance lock — clicking the QQ icon again on a desktop that already has one running just focuses the existing window, it doesn't start a second process. The lock file lives at `$HOME/.config/QQ/SingletonLock`, so the solution is to give each instance its &#x2A;*own `HOME`**."},"308":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-102","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#running-multiple-qq-accounts","content":"SnowLuma needs no extra configuration: HookManager walks every QQ main process it can find, injects the hook into each, and spins up a separate `OneBotInstance` per UIN with its own `config/onebot_<uin>.json`."},"309":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-103","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#launch-a-second-qq-from-the-novnc-desktop","content":"Open a terminal inside the noVNC desktop (right-click the taskbar / launch `xterm` / use the in-container terminal shortcut)."},"310":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-104","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#launch-a-second-qq-from-the-novnc-desktop","content":"Start a new QQ under an isolated `HOME`:"},"311":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-105","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#launch-a-second-qq-from-the-novnc-desktop","content":"A fresh QQ login window appears — scan-login or password-login the second account."},"312":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-106","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#launch-a-second-qq-from-the-novnc-desktop","content":"SnowLuma auto-injects the hook and stands up a per-UIN OneBot instance."},"313":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-107","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#launch-a-second-qq-from-the-novnc-desktop","content":"`disown` detaches the QQ process from the terminal so closing the terminal won't kill it."},"314":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-108","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#persisting-across-container-restarts","content":"`/app/qq-acct2` is an in-container path; recreating the container wipes it. Mount a dedicated volume per extra account in `docker-compose.yml`:"},"315":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-109","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#persisting-across-container-restarts","content":"After that, bringing the second account up only takes the same one-liner in the noVNC terminal:"},"316":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-110","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#auto-starting-every-account-on-boot","content":"Save the script to a persisted volume, e.g. `/app/snowluma-data/start-extra-qq.sh`:"},"317":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-111","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#auto-starting-every-account-on-boot","content":"Hook it into the desktop's autostart (XFCE: drop a `.desktop` into `~/.config/autostart/`) for an in-DE solution, or add a new program block to `supervisord.conf` and rebuild the image for a more reliable boot-up wire."},"318":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-112","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#caveats","content":"**One HOME per QQ instance** — never share a `HOME` between two QQs; they'll fight over the lock file."},"319":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-113","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#caveats","content":"**Resources**: each QQ is a full Chromium process, \\~300-500 MB RAM. The default `--shm-size=1g` is fine for one; bump to `2gb`+ for multi-account."},"320":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-114","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#caveats","content":"**All windows share the same Xvfb desktop**: noVNC shows every QQ window; minimize the ones you've already logged into. Hook keeps working regardless of window state."},"321":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-115","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#caveats","content":"**WebUI lists every UIN automatically**: no manual configuration — SnowLuma surfaces each new account in the WebUI and `get_login_info` returns the new UINs once login completes."},"322":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-116","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#auto-injection","content":"The image defaults to `SNOWLUMA_HOOK_AUTOLOAD=1`: when the container starts, the hook is injected into the QQ process in passive-observe mode. Once you scan-login, the hook auto-promotes to working mode. supervisor also restarts QQ on crash through the same flow."},"323":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-117","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#turning-it-off","content":"If you prefer the legacy \"manual Load via WebUI\" workflow:"},"324":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-118","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#turning-it-off","content":"Or set `SNOWLUMA_HOOK_AUTOLOAD: 0` in `docker-compose.yml`, or edit `/app/snowluma-data/config/runtime.json` inside the volume to `\"hookAutoLoad\": false`. Environment variables win."},"325":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-119","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#common-ops","content":"Shell into the container:"},"326":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-120","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","ta